---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Litia — The future of learning"
  description="Litia reads, counts, and writes along with learners like nothing ever seen before."
>
  <style>
    /* Bouncy entrance animation when the page loads */
    .animate-pop {
      opacity: 0;
      transform: translateY(40px) scale(0.9);
      animation: popIn 0.7s cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1) forwards;
    }
    /* Stagger the animations so they load one after another */
    .delay-1 { animation-delay: 0.1s; }
    .delay-2 { animation-delay: 0.2s; }
    .delay-3 { animation-delay: 0.3s; }

    @keyframes popIn {
      to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0) scale(1); }
    }

    /* Edge-to-edge image card styling */
    .screenshot-card {
      padding: 0; /* Removes padding so the image touches the borders */
      overflow: hidden;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
    }
    
    .screenshot-img-wrapper {
      overflow: hidden; /* Keeps the zooming image inside the curved borders */
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
    }
    
    .screenshot-img {
      width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      display: block;
      transition: transform 0.6s cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1);
    }
    
    .screenshot-card:hover .screenshot-img {
      transform: scale(1.08) rotate(-3deg); 
    }
    
    .screenshot-caption {
      padding: 16px;
      font-weight: 800;
      text-align: center;
      color: var(--text);
      background: var(--surface);
    }
  </style>

  <section class="hero">
    <div>
      <h1>Litia is the future of learning.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Litia reads, counts, writes, and more along with learners as they build
        literacy and mathematical skills.
      </p>

      <div class="ctaRow">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${Astro.base || ''}/contact`}>Request a demo</a>
        <a class="button" href={`${Astro.base || ''}/educators`}>Learn more</a>
      </div>

      <div class="cardGrid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Real technology to teach real skills</h3>
          <p>No ads. No AI or LLMs stealing your data. No cloud storage required. No personal information is retained or sold!</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Multilayered learning</h3>
          <p>Eye tracking builds neural connections across letters, phonemes, words, and mathematics. Reading, writing, and basic calculations are taught.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Progress you can trust</h3>
          <p>Progress dashboards and datasets are available for adults and educators displaying information about their students' success.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>What it does</h3>
          <p>Litia gives students quizzes for literacy and arithmetic development, vocabulary flashcards, and interactive reading.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p></p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top: 64px;">
    <h2>Inside the App</h2>
    <p class="subtle" style="margin-bottom: 24px;">Take a peek at how Litia makes foundational learning fun.</p>
    
    <div class="cardGrid">
      <div class="card screenshot-card animate-pop delay-1">
        <div class="screenshot-img-wrapper">
          <img src="/home-screen.png" alt="Litia Home Screen" class="screenshot-img" />
        </div>
        <div class="screenshot-caption">Guided Pathways</div>
      </div>

      <div class="card screenshot-card animate-pop delay-2">
        <div class="screenshot-img-wrapper">
          <img src="/quiz-screen.png" alt="Litia Quiz Interaction" class="screenshot-img" />
        </div>
        <div class="screenshot-caption">Eye-Tracked Quizzes</div>
      </div>

      <div class="card screenshot-card animate-pop delay-3">
        <div class="screenshot-img-wrapper">
          <img src="/drawing-screen.png" alt="Litia Creative Drawing" class="screenshot-img" />
        </div>
        <div class="screenshot-caption">Creative Rewards</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-top: 64px;" class="prose">
    <h2>How the experience works</h2>
    <p>
      Quizzes use eye tracking on iOS devices to identify the letter, phoneme,
      or word a learner looks at. The app highlights the item, displays an
      associated image, and speaks the word before the learner selects the
      matching term for the prompt.
    </p>
    <p>
      Story mode reads along with the learner while they track text on screen,
      and the vocabulary pathway uses gaze-guided flashcards to build rapid
      recognition across languages.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
